 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Though, in a little walk by Dublin,\nThe ruddy sunbreaks the wondrous fire;\nI have seen it softly gone below them,\nAnd left him, to let his memory live.\nHe never was: \"Nothing's more divine\nThan the rest when they are all apart.\"[793a. A\nThere's no doubt that you'll find me fond again,\nWhen evening is over and I'm alone;\nYou'll be glad at last of Nature's delight,\nIn her calm retreat on the terrace.\nSo, now for us who, like so many these,\nShall return from Dublin we will agree",
